    "steps": [
        {
            "step_number": 1,
            "title": "Assembling Parabolic Solar Cooker Tripod Base Stand",
            "content": [
                "Insert a 14mm bolt through each tripod leg and through the center plate. Secure each bolt by hand threading a nut on the other side.",
                "Be sure the flat side of each tripod leg is facing toward the ground."
            ],
            "images": [
                "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/S5t4IEIkgIJkGa1a.medium",
                "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/KjghqbuhrxDthMTV.medium"
            ],
            "images_200x150": [
                "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/S5t4IEIkgIJkGa1a.200x150",
                "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/KjghqbuhrxDthMTV.200x150"
            ],
            "edit_url": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/edit/19229/54251",
            "comments_count": 0,
            "add_comment_url": null
        },
        {
            "step_number": 2,
            "content": [
                "Tighten each nut using two 14mm wrenches until each leg is stable and the tripod will stand on its own."
            ],
            "image": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/3itKW3sgtw4jrIM6.medium",
            "edit_url": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/edit/19229/54252",
            "comments_count": 0,
            "add_comment_url": null
        }
    ],
    "conclusion": "To disassemble your device, follow these instructions in reverse order.",
